      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe limit for acetaminophen.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6000 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 4000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. At 6 g/day, there is a serious risk of hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg.\n\nHere are some options, depending on what you intended:\n1. **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3000 mg/day). This may be what you meant.\n2. **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4000 mg/day). This is the standard maximum.\n3. **650 mg by mouth four times daily**, or another regimen you prefer.\n\nTell me which regimen you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 2000 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still recommend a pharmacy review in that case."
      }
     ],
